{"drhp":{"anchor_allotment":null,"as_of":"","board":[{"designation":"Chairman","independent":false,"name":"Onkar Kanwar"},{"designation":"Vice Chairman & Managing Director","independent":false,"name":"Neeraj Kanwar"},{"designation":"Director","independent":false,"name":"Sumit Dayal"},{"designation":"Chief Financial Officer & Whole-time Director","independent":false,"name":"Gaurav Kumar"},{"designation":"Independent Director","independent":true,"name":"Francesco Crispino"}],"business":"Apollo Tyres Ltd manufactures and sells automotive tyres under the Apollo Tyres and Vredestein brands. Its product portfolio spans passenger vehicles, commercial vehicles, two-wheelers, off-highway vehicles, and light trucks, catering to both original equipment manufacturers (OEMs) and the replacement market. The company operates manufacturing facilities in India and Europe, supported by global R&D centers and a wide distribution network.","certs":"ISCC+ Certification|ISO 20400:2017 (Sustainable Procurement)|EcoVadis Gold Rating (98th percentile)|SBTi validation for near-term and net-zero emissions reduction targets|IGBC Green Existing Building Certification (Apollo House, Gurugram)|British Safety Council Sword of Honour (Chennai and Limda …","co":"APOLLO TYRES LTD","depth":"deep","end_markets":"India (OEM and replacement)|Europe (premium and replacement)|Americas (premium and all-weather)|Global exports to over 100 countries","expansion":"The Company continued to invest in its modern, highly automated manufacturing facilities across India and Europe, which provide a strong foundation for cost-competitive production and support growth across both domestic and international markets. The state-of-the-art facility in Andhra Pradesh was highlighted during the Apollo Tyres Global Partners' Summit in February 2026, showcasing the scale, advanced technology, and operational discipline driving the next phase of growth. No new specific capex projects with commissioning or completion timelines were disclosed.","grades":{"rel":0,"s":"","wm90":null},"industry":"Auto Components","isin":"INE438A01022","kpi":null,"listed_on":"","litigation":{"as_of":"","material":false,"note":"The Competition Commission of India (CCI) found the Company, along with other tyre manufacturers, to have contravened Section 3 of the Competition Act, 2002, and imposed a penalty. The Company appealed to NCLAT, which remanded the matter back to CCI. CCI has appealed to the Supreme Court. As of the report date, no penalty amount is enforceable against/payable by the Company."},"mdna":"India: strong economic growth (GDP ~7.6%), record vehicle sales, improving consumer demand, and structural shift towards premium and high-value consumption.|India tyre demand expected to grow 6-8% during FY26, driven by improving affordability, favourable rural demand, and strengthening replacement segment.|Europe: modest recovery in passenger vehicle demand but continued pressure from weak industrial activity, heightened competitive intensity, and supply chain disruptions.|Europe: subdued demand across key segments, increased imports, and higher energy costs intensifying competitive …","objects":null,"oem":"","one_liner":"Apollo Tyres is a global tyre manufacturer with a dual-brand strategy (Apollo Tyres and Vredestein), serving over 100 countries across mass, premium, and luxury segments.","peer_panel":{"asof":"2026-08-14","industry":"Auto Components","peers":[{"ebitda_margin":19.1,"fy":"FY26","growth_basis":"3y CAGR","mcap":67614,"name":"Schaeffler India Limited","pat":1196.2,"pat_growth":10.8,"pe":56.5,"rev":9395.3,"rev_growth":11.0,"s":"SCHAEFFLER","source":"drhp","why":"named in DRHP"},{"ebitda_margin":11.4,"fy":"FY26","growth_basis":"7y CAGR","mcap":64746,"name":"Uno Minda Limited","pat":1284.1,"pat_growth":24.0,"pe":50.4,"rev":19657.6,"rev_growth":18.7,"s":"UNOMINDA","source":"drhp","why":"named in DRHP"},{"ebitda_margin":25.2,"fy":"FY26","growth_basis":"6y CAGR","mcap":32022,"name":"Sona BLW Precisi